"""
Stacking Ensemble with Meta-Learner — two mediocre models can beat one good one.

WHAT IT DOES: Stacking trains base models, then trains a meta-model on their
predictions: it learns when to trust which base. This pattern demonstrates the full
loop: fit bases → generate out-of-fold predictions → fit meta → compare accuracies
(stack should match or beat the best base). Uses two simple threshold classifiers as
base models and a linear meta-learner.

WHEN TO USE: Combining diverse base models where you suspect different models excel
on different regions of the data. The meta-learner learns the weighting automatically
— you don't have to guess which model to trust when.

GUARANTEES: Stacking accuracy beats the average of base model accuracies on the test
set. The meta-learner is trained on out-of-fold predictions (not the training
predictions the base models saw), preventing overfitting.

NOT: A production stacking implementation. No cross-validation for the meta-learner's
own parameters, no regularization, no support for more than two base models. The
shipped version has NO input validation — NaN in X trains silently with output
identical to a clean run (AURA-E008).
"""
